{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c63d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a986-16d4-7923-b79d-f784beb66015"},"sequence":377,"recorded_at":1780531400000749,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f870b610-f41f-4227-a805-61cb8ebcb67d","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"f870b610-f41f-4227-a805-61cb8ebcb67d","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f870b610-f41f-4227-a805-61cb8ebcb67d"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0a986-f7e5-7de3-91bb-417ac0bc458b"},"task_id":"01a0a986-f7e5-7de3-91bb-417ac0bc458b","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0a986-f7e5-7de3-91bb-417ac0bc458b","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/r2-evidence/outcome.md`.\n1|# TASK-260916-304bw2 — catalog lifecycle and polished UI (developer outcome)\n2|\n3|Status: ready for review (board `to-review`).\n4|\n5|## Follow-up fix (checklist item 15): manual autostart defect\n6|\n7|Manual CUA smoke found the detail toggle showing login ON for the manual org\n8|runner while `~/Library/LaunchAgents/actions.runner.*` does not exist:\n9|external `manual-service.plist` RunAtLoad=true controls bootstrap startup\n10|only, never login persistence. Fixed model: effective login (`loginEnabled`)\n11|is ON for external manual services only with a matching\n12|`~/Library/LaunchAgents/<label>.plist` registration (RunAtLoad true, same\n13|label/directory/runsvc); standard manifests use their own RunAtLoad. The\n14|toggle now really registers/unregisters login (copy in/out of LaunchAgents),\n15|never edits the external service file, never bootstraps/bootouts (live state\n16|preserved), refuses foreign same-label plists in both directions, and relink\n17|carries a managed registration to the new directory. Detail shows the toggle\n18|bound to effective login plus the preserved external RunAtLoad as info.\n19|Production fixture untouched (verified: no `actions.runner.*` in\n20|`~/Library/LaunchAgents`, both runners still `running`). Candidate left UNCOMMITTED in the\n21|Story worktree for handoff snapshot; no producer commits on the Story branch.\n22|\n23|## What shipped\n24|\n25|Universal persistent catalog (`catalog.json`, versioned, no secrets), manual +\n26|standard LaunchAgent discovery/import with unsupported read-only kinds,\n27|user-folder import, canonical dedupe, no-space relocation (no auto-move),\n28|Local/Remote/Operation separation with truthful busy/stale/offline UI,\n29|individual + bulk power with confirmed stop, manifest/stdout/stderr + `_diag`\n30|log access with redaction, independent app/runner login policies, explicit\n31|unregister (typed, stopped-only, server/scope/ID+path bound, shared installer\n32|lease) distinct from entry-only catalog removal, fresh API group membership\n33|(not stale `.runner` pool) with an in-app post-registration repository editor\n34|(owned apply + shared takeover, stale refusal, exact confirmation), full menu +\n35|management-window UI, README universal onboarding, 1.2.0 signed candidate.\n36|\n37|No SSH fleet controls. No stop-after-job. No new delegates. Release machinery\n38|(`Scripts/release*`, workflows, `RELEASING.md`) untouched.\n39|\n40|## UI entry points (manual verification, no UI tests per task)\n41|\n42|- Menu (400pt): per-row Enable / Disable… buttons, per-row lock, GitHub\n43|  signature line, bottom Enable all / Disable all… / Add runner… / Runners and\n44|  settings…. Updates + Quit live only in Settings. Icon: outline/filled/error\n45|  with textual accessibility label.\n46|- Management window → Runners → select org runner → Repository access →\n47|  Load current access → checkboxes → Apply (owned) or Take over and apply\n48|  (shared/imported). Repo runners show per-repo note (no groups).\n49|- Detail: directory, work folder, controller kind, service label, agent ID,\n50|  labels, RunAtLoad toggle (preserved policy), log tail, rename, relink moved\n51|  folder, Remove from app (entry only, warns when running), Unregister from\n52|  GitHub (typed, stopped-only).\n53|\n54|## AC coverage: 18 of 19 rows driven (row 18 is the stated manual-UI bound)\n55|\n56|| # | AC row | Production call site | Named test(s) |\n57||---|--------|----------------------|---------------|\n58|| 1 | Persistent catalog, rename-safe identity | `RunnerCatalogStore.add/load` | `catalogPersistsAndDedupesCanonicalViaSymlink`, `aliasDoesNotChangeIdentity` |\n59|| 2 | Manual + standard discovery, unsupported read-only, no auto-launch | `RunnerDiscovery.discoverCandidates`, `Runners.Flow.apply(.importCandidate)` | `discoveryFindsManualAndStandardWithoutLaunching`, `importPreservesServiceAndRunAtLoad`, `importRefusesUnsupportedWithoutSecondProcess`, `unsupportedShowsStateButRefusesControl` |\n60|| 3 | User folders + dedupe (symlink collapse; same name ≠ same runner) | `RunnerDiscovery.validateFolder`, `RunnerCatalogStore.add` | `catalogPersistsAndDedupesCanonicalViaSymlink`, `catalogKeepsSameNameDifferentScopesAsTwoRunners` |\n61|| 4 | No-space validation, relocation, no auto-move | `RunnersCatalogGates.validateImportable` | `importRefusesSpacedPathWithoutMoving`, `importGateRefusesSpacedPathDirectly` |\n62|| 5 | Local/remote/operation separation | `LaunchAgentService.snapshots`, `Runners.State.reduce(.refreshed)` | `snapshotsPreserveRunningDespiteMissingRunner`, `refreshRemoteKeepsLocalOnOffline` |\n63|| 6 | Truthful busy/stale/offline | `GitHubRunnerObserver.match/isStale/withFreshness`, `Runners.StopConfirmation` | `observerMatchesByIDNeverByName`, `observerRefusesContradictionAndForeignName`, `staleBusyFalseIsNotIdleProof` |\n64|| 7 | Individual/bulk power, per-row errors, no duplicates | `Runners.Flow.apply(.setEnabled/.setEnabledMany)`, `LaunchAgentService.setEnabled` | `bulkPowerReportsPartialFailuresPerRow`, `offlineLocalControlWithoutToken` (+ existing `startIsIdempotent…`) |\n65|| 8 | Stop despite missing `.runner`; bad manifest blocks start | `LaunchAgentService.setEnabled` | `stopWorksDespiteMissingRunnerStartBlockedOnBadManifest`, `snapshotsPreserveRunningDespiteMissingRunner` |\n66|| 9 | Log access from manifest + `_diag`, redacted, bounded | `RunnerDiagnostics.logFiles/tail` | `diagnosticsResolvesManifestPathsAndRedacts` |\n67|| 10 | Independent login policies, preserved, separate change | `RunnerCatalogStore` (`runAtLoad`), `Runners.Flow.apply(.setRunAtLoad)` | `importPreservesServiceAndRunAtLoad`, `standardPolicyChangePreservesManifestAndSkipsLaunchctl` |\n68|| 10b | Effective manual login: external RunAtLoad=true ⇒ OFF; toggle really registers/unregisters; live state preserved; foreign refused | `RunnerControllers.effectiveLogin`, `Runners.Flow.apply(.setRunAtLoad)` + `setManualLogin`, `LaunchAgentService.snapshots` | `manualExternalRunAtLoadTrueDisplaysLoginOff`, `standardManifestShowsActualPolicy`, `manualToggleOnRegistersLoginWithoutChangingLiveState`, `manualToggleOffUnregistersLoginWithoutStopping`, `manualToggleRefusesForeignPlist` |\n69|| 11 | Unregister vs remove, shared lease, busy + retry | `Runners.Flow.apply(.removeFromApp/.unregister)`, `RunnerInstallerService.unregister` | `removeDeletesOnlyEntryAndWarnsWhenRunning`, `unregisterRefuses*` (4), `unregisterRemovesRemoteKeepsFilesAndEntry`, `installerLeaseSerializesUnregisterAndInstall` |\n70|| 12 | Preserve policies + existing runners; restart ≠ enable | `RunnerCatalogStore.migrateIfNeeded`, import path (no bootstrap) | `migrationPreservesPoliciesWithoutTouchingServices`, `importPreservesServiceAndRunAtLoad` |\n71|| 13 | Production installs unaffected, no duplicate process | migration + idempotent start + live `launchctl print` | `migrationPreservesPoliciesWithoutTouchingServices` + live check (both `state = running`, one process each) |\n72|| 14 | Local works offline; API failures don't change/hide local | `Runners.Flow.apply(.refreshRemote/.setEnabled)` | `refreshRemoteKeepsLocalOnOffline`, `offlineLocalControlWithoutToken` |\n73|| 15 | Fresh API group membership, never stale pool, no same-name adoption | `Runners.Flow.resolveFreshGroup`, `GitHubRunnerAPIClient.fetchGroupRunners` | `groupAccessUsesFreshAPIMembershipNotStalePool` |\n74|| 16 | In-app repo editor: owned apply, shared takeover, stale refusal, exact confirm, repo refused | `Runners.Flow.apply(.loadGroupAccess/.applyGroupAccess)` | `applyGroupAccessRequiresTakeoverForShared`, `applyGroupAccessRefusesStaleGroup`, `applyGroupAccessConfirmsExactRepos`, `groupAccessRefusesRepoScope` |\n75|| 18 | Full UI integrated (menu, detail, editor, login toggle, no fleet/stop-after-job) | — (bound) | BOUND: manual via signed candidate (no UI tests per task) |\n76|| 19 | Tests pass + native app builds (1.2.0) | `swift test`, `Scripts/build.sh` | exit 0 (197 tests) + exit 0 `BUILD SUCCEEDED` + `codesign --verify` exit 0 |\n77|\n78|## Mutant evidence: 17 narrowing, 0 survivors\n79|\n80|Each mutant keeps its gate and admits exactly one rejected member; the named\n81|test fails (exit 1). Tree reverted after each run; final suite green.\n82|\n83|| Mutant | Narrows the gate to | Named failing test |\n84||--------|---------------------|--------------------|\n85|| `catalog-dedupe-admits-alias-label` | Dedupe on dir+label (admits same dir, other label) | `catalogPersistsAndDedupesCanonicalViaSymlink` |\n86|| `import-admits-spaced-path` | No-space on work only (admits spaced install path) | `importGateRefusesSpacedPathDirectly` |\n87|| `manifest-admits-wrong-directory` | Manifest on label+args (admits wrong WorkingDirectory) | `stopWorksDespiteMissingRunnerStartBlockedOnBadManifest` |\n88|| `unsupported-admits-stop` | Unsupported refuses start only (admits stop) | `unsupportedShowsStateButRefusesControl` |\n89|| `observer-adopts-foreign-name` | Observer falls back to same-name foreign ID | `observerRefusesContradictionAndForeignName` |\n90|| `stale-admits-idle` | Stale treats busy=false as fresh | `staleBusyFalseIsNotIdleProof` |\n91|| `unregister-admits-wrong-confirmation` | Confirmation accepts the wrong lit